lisa-design:
- RepoState.Detail stays one string, written as Markdown (PR refs via PRLink = [repo#n](https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>/pull/n)); SlackText converts those links to <url|label> when the detail goes to Slack (hold messages, dry-run plan). Rejected: storing two renderings or a template token in the persisted state.
- Owner is Engine config (Engine.Owner from --owner) and a Render parameter, not persisted in State: no state schema change, and trains already open (issue #63 from main) parse unchanged. PRLink without an owner falls back to the plain "repo#n" label, never a bare "#n".
- Hold dedupe keys include Detail, so the first run of this version re-posts each currently held repo once (detail text changed). Accepted: one-time, and the mock train is the only open one.
- Closed-PR handling in notify lives in Decide (ReasonNone when pull_request.state == closed), so plan, post and the needs-human rule (Route calls Decide) all drop the run with one rule. A recovery reply for an incident open on a now-closed PR is intentionally not posted (spec: no reply).
- Workflows: every job of the kind CI workflows gets a job-level if with the same guard; required becomes ${{ always() && !(closed) }} so it is skipped (non-failure) on a closed PR and unchanged on open PRs/pushes. ci-common jobs and release-checks are guarded too (release-checks re-runs on the relabelled merged release PR as well). Guards are pinned by TestClosedPRGuard in internal/ciworkflows.

